    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1438">

                <pb facs="1265" n="1007" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg1007"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 16, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>977. This Government will undertake the work requested by the British Government
                    in your 1474 in accordance with the plan outlined in the Department’s 963 of
                    yesterday, and Gerard has been instructed to present the matter to the German
                    Government and report.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
